\f3\b\fs28 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Not yet to separate platform-specific performances
\f0\b0 , elaborate multichat productions, or scheduling work around Kick's advanced Partner incentives.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 I think we have arrived at a sensible production strategy:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 One creative process. Multiple broadcast endpoints. Multiple voluntary payment paths. One accumulating research record.
\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 You may well discover that different platforms attract different kinds of people: YouTube viewers curious about experiments, Kick viewers interested in your personality and live conversation, Patreon supporters invested in the continuation of the entire undertaking.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 That's a hypothesis worth testing, not an assumption I'd build the whole enterprise around.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 And most importantly, you don't need to significantly change what happens at the workbench to run that experiment.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 The expensive part is your time and attention. The additional broadcast signal is comparatively cheap.\cf0 \cb1 \
