\cf2 \cb5 These are self-selected anecdotes, not representative survey data. But they suggest two practical considerations:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 First, Kick may attract a greater proportion of viewers who regard provocation as entertainment.
\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Second, the host's willingness to establish and enforce a community culture makes a substantial difference.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 For your program, I actually think that distinction is encouraging.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 You're not trying to host a polite academic seminar exclusively. Your own material includes absurdist comedy, philosophical challenges, unusually ambitious propositions, and an interest in lively disagreement.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Some amount of irreverence is compatible with that.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 What wouldn't be compatible is allowing the stream to become dominated by people trying to provoke an emotional reaction at the expense of the inventive work.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

