\cf2 \cb5 For your program I'd favor open chat initially, with automatic spam filtering and a short set of explicit norms.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Something along the lines of:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb5 Welcome to the Wilder-ness. Unusual ideas, serious questions, absurd humor, and constructive disagreement are welcome. Personal harassment, spam, doxxing, and demands for attention are not. Wilder may be busy inventing stuff. Chat happens when it happens. 
\f2 \uc0\u9774 \u65039 
\f0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 I would also avoid reacting to every hostile remark. Rewarding provocations with extended attention can make them an increasingly significant part of the production.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 And there's no inherent reason your stream needs to resemble Kick's most spectacular personalities.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 A recognizable, extremely calm inventor casually attempting something wildly ambitious could be distinctive precisely because it contrasts with the high-energy programming.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 The unanswered question is whether enough Kick viewers would choose to spend time with that experience.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 That's something a real multicast experiment can establish much better than platform-level statistics.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

